### Tone: End-of-game award: Near Miss, the most answers within twice the truth (at least two). $count: those answers.
### Close, never quite there; mock-sympathetic, nearly kind.

award-near-miss-1 =
    The Near Miss award goes to { $name }: { $count ->
        [one] one answer
       *[other] { $count } answers
    } within twice the truth. Close. Not close enough. But close.
award-near-miss-2 = { $name }, almost right, over and over. If “almost” scored points, you’d have won. It scores some. Not enough.
award-near-miss-3 = Near Miss: { $name }. You keep landing just next to the truth. Like a moth near a lamp.
award-near-miss-4 = { $name } got close so often that the truth started to feel watched.
award-near-miss-5 = The award for nearly is presented to { $name }. Nearly impressive. Nearly.
award-near-miss-6 = { $name }, within a factor of two, again and again. Respectable. The kind of respectable nobody writes songs about.
award-near-miss-7 = Near Miss: { $name }. The bullseye was right there. You could see it. You just didn’t hit it.
award-near-miss-8 = { $name } kept finishing just outside the target. A consistent, honourable, slightly frustrating near miss.
award-near-miss-9 = The Near Miss goes to { $name }. I’d say better luck next time, but luck isn’t the problem. Probably.
award-near-miss-10 = { $name }: close, every time. I find it oddly moving. I find most things oddly moving when I’m winning.
